# /home/user/ar0xOS/config/packages.x86_64
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PHASE 3 — canonical ar0x package list for the archiso 92 `iso` buildmode.
# One package (or package group) per line. Lines starting with # and blank
# lines are ignored; inline trailing comments are stripped by mkarchiso.
#
# ⚠️ MANDATORY (archiso 92, docs/README.profile.rst): `mkinitcpio` AND
#    `mkinitcpio-archiso` must be present, or the live initramfs will not boot.
# ⚠️ MANDATORY (archiso 92, mkarchiso::_validate_requirements_bootmode_bios.syslinux):
#    `syslinux` must be IN THIS LIST, not only installed on the host — mkarchiso
#    copies isolinux.bin / *.c32 out of the *airootfs*, not the host.
# ⚠️ `grub` is needed in the airootfs so Calamares (Phase 10) can install GRUB
#    onto the target disk from the live system's own package files.
#
# This is the PHASE 3 BASE set only. Later phases APPEND their own sections:
#   Phase 4 : plymouth (ADDED), GRUB/Plymouth/syslinux themes
#   Phase 5 : tzdata, rtkit + 23 config/system/** drop-ins (apparmor already present)
#   Phase 6 : 37 packages — Hyprland Lua stack, SDDM Qt6 theme, GTK3/GTK4,
#             Qt5/Qt6, icons/cursors/fonts, wallpapers, /etc/skel dotfiles
#   Phase 7 : screenfetch (official [extra] 3.9.9-1). neofetch is AUR-only
#             (removed from [extra] upstream, RISK-010) and is NOT on the ISO;
#             its config IS shipped for post-install use.
#   Phase 8 : ar0x-welcome ar0x-update ar0x-info ar0x-theme ar0x-meta ...
#   Phase 10: calamares 3.4.3 (from the [ar0x] repo, ADR-017)
# Phase 11 rebuilds the ISO from the accumulated list. Phase 3's own build is
# a BASE BOOTSTRAP SMOKE TEST, not the final release ISO.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Base system -------------------------------------------------------------
base
arch-install-scripts
linux-lts
linux-lts-headers
linux-firmware
intel-ucode
amd-ucode
wireless-regdb
sof-firmware

# --- Live initramfs (MANDATORY for archiso) ----------------------------------
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso

# --- Bootloaders / disk utilities (must exist inside the airootfs) -----------
plymouth
grub
syslinux
edk2-shell
efibootmgr
dosfstools
mtools
e2fsprogs
btrfs-progs
xfsprogs
f2fs-tools
exfatprogs
gptfdisk
parted
cryptsetup
lvm2
squashfs-tools

# --- Core userspace / init ---------------------------------------------------
# Phase 5 additions: tzdata (locale/timezone) + rtkit (PipeWire realtime
# scheduling). apparmor, nftables, sudo and polkit were already in the Phase 3
# base set — do NOT add them twice.
tzdata
rtkit
sudo
polkit
networkmanager
nftables
apparmor
dbus
gnupg
openssh
pacman-contrib
reflector

# --- Audio (PipeWire stack; config/ arrives in Phase 5) ---------------------
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
pipewire-jack
wireplumber
alsa-utils
bluez
bluez-utils

# --- Graphics baseline (full DE stack arrives in Phase 6) -------------------
mesa
vulkan-icd-loader

# --- Networking / firmware tools ---------------------------------------------
iw
wpa_supplicant
ethtool
usbutils
pciutils

# --- Developer baseline (audience = Developers) -----------------------------
git
base-devel
neovim
zsh
zsh-completions
starship
bash-completion
man-db
man-pages
less
which
curl
wget
rsync
jq
tmux

# --- Phase 6: Wayland desktop (Hyprland 0.57 + SDDM 0.21) -------------------
# HARD pins (hyprland 0.57.1 et al.) resolve from [ar0x] FIRST in
# config/pacman.conf.build (ADR-017); until Phase 9 builds them, the frozen
# 2026/11/01 [extra] snapshot supplies 0.57.0-3. Both are Lua-config releases.
# Only official [core]/[extra] packages are named here — NO AUR (RISK-010).
hyprland
hyprpaper
hyprlock
hypridle
waybar
sddm
xorg-xwayland
xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
qt5-wayland
qt6-wayland
qt5ct
qt6ct
gtk3
gtk4
libadwaita
papirus-icon-theme
adwaita-icon-theme
adwaita-cursors
inter-font
ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-emoji
kitty
wofi
mako
thunar
gvfs
grim
slurp
wl-clipboard
brightnessctl
playerctl
network-manager-applet
polkit-gnome
xdg-user-dirs
fastfetch

# --- Phase 7: branded fetch tools -------------------------------------------
# fastfetch (above) is the default. screenfetch is in Arch [extra] and gets the
# ar0x-screenfetch wrapper + custom Xcursor-coloured ASCII art. neofetch is
# deliberately ABSENT: AUR-only, upstream archived (RISK-010).
screenfetch
